outputs.L1:
A user device (200) comprising a display (206), an interface (208) configured to communicate with a lamp comprising controllable light sources (104), and a processor (202) configured to execute an application (214), wherein the application is configured to:

- control the lamp to emit light in accordance with a source light pattern (302), the source light pattern defining, for each light source, the light to be emitted by that light source and designating at least one of the light sources as a marker light source (308);
- receive an image, captured by a camera (210), of the source light pattern as projected by the lamp onto a target surface (300), wherein a target light pattern (310) in the image is distorted;
- display the received image on the display;
- detect locations in the displayed image at which the marker light source or sources are positioned or intended to emit light onto the target surface; and
- use the detected locations of the marker light source or sources to align a control overlay with the displayed image, the control overlay identifying, for each light source, an area in the displayed image onto which that light source is intended to emit light, wherein the control overlay enables a user of the user device to control the light sources in response to at least one user selection.

counterfactuals.output:
**1. A user device for controlling a multi-source lamp, the user device comprising:**

a communication interface configured to communicate with the multi-source lamp, the multi-source lamp comprising a plurality of individually controllable light sources configured to collectively project a light pattern and a plurality of marker light sources configured to project respective optical markers having predetermined spatial relationships to the light pattern;

a camera configured to capture an image of a surface onto which the light pattern and the optical markers are projected;

a display;

a user input interface; and

one or more processors configured to:

identify, in the image, image locations of the respective optical markers;

determine, based on differences between the image locations and expected locations corresponding to the predetermined spatial relationships, a geometric transformation representing distortion of the projected light pattern in the image;

apply the geometric transformation to align an interactive control overlay with the projected light pattern depicted in the image;

cause the display to present the image with the aligned interactive control overlay;

receive, via the user input interface, a user interaction with a region of the interactive control overlay corresponding to at least one of the individually controllable light sources; and

transmit, via the communication interface and responsive to the user interaction, a control command that causes the multi-source lamp to modify light emitted by the at least one individually controllable light source.

1. **A display-equipped device comprising:**

a display;

a communication interface configured to communicate with a controllable lamp;

an image interface configured to receive, from a camera, an image depicting a projection produced by the controllable lamp on a projection surface, the projection appearing geometrically distorted in the image and including a plurality of designated marker lights;

a user-input interface; and

one or more processors configured to:

identify respective image locations of the plurality of designated marker lights in the image;

determine, based on the respective image locations, a registration mapping between the projection depicted in the image and a coordinate system of the display;

display the image on the display;

register, according to the registration mapping, a user-control overlay with the projection depicted in the displayed image;

receive, via the user-input interface, a user interaction with the user-control overlay; and

cause the communication interface to transmit, to the controllable lamp, a control command determined from the user interaction.

1. **A computer-implemented method performed by a mobile computing device**, the method comprising:  
capturing an image of an environment containing illumination produced by a plurality of controllable light sources and a plurality of marker lights having known spatial positions;  
detecting respective image positions of the marker lights in the captured image;  
determining, from the known spatial positions and the detected image positions, a spatial transformation that compensates for geometric distortion between a reference coordinate system and the captured image;  
using the spatial transformation to map respective projected areas associated with the controllable light sources to corresponding regions of the captured image;  
displaying, over the captured image, an interactive graphical overlay aligned with the corresponding regions;  
receiving a user interaction with a portion of the interactive graphical overlay corresponding to a selected projected area; and  
causing at least one controllable light source associated with the selected projected area to change an illumination parameter.
